<div class="declaration-body">
  <p class="declaration-basis">in accordance with ED Decision 2022/024/R and the attached Technical Specification for ADS-L transmissions using the SRD-860 frequency band (&ldquo;ADS-L 4 SRD 860&rdquo;)</p>

  <p>The undersigned, representing the manufacturer:</p>
  <p class="declaration-indent">François Catuhe EI<br>23 cours de Verdun, 33000 Bordeaux, France</p>

  <p>declares under sole responsibility that the following product:</p>
  <dl class="declaration-indent">
    <dt>Product Name</dt>
    <dd>skyBlip Go</dd>
    <dt>Hardware Reference</dt>
    <dd>Brand LILYGO, model T-Echo, 868&nbsp;MHz, with BME280</dd>
    <dt>Firmware Version</dt>
    <dd>skyBlip v1, with ADS-L protocol v1</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>is in conformity with the ADS-L 4 SRD860 Standard Issue 2</p>
  <div class="declaration-scope">
    <p>The manufacturer supplies the firmware. This declaration covers it on one hardware, the LilyGO T-Echo, which has passed CE testing. The manufacturer will revise this declaration before supporting any other hardware.</p>
    <p>At every start-up the firmware checks that the radio and the barometer answer. If either does not, the unit does not run: it neither transmits nor receives, and it cannot be activated.</p>
  </div>

  <p>The device operates on the following transmission parameters:</p>
  <dl class="declaration-indent">
    <dt>Transmission Bands and Power Levels</dt>
    <dd>M-band only, on 868.2&nbsp;MHz and 868.4&nbsp;MHz. Transmit power set to 14&nbsp;dBm (25&nbsp;mW), within the M-band limit of 14&nbsp;dBm e.r.p. Nothing is transmitted on the O-band.</dd>
    <dt>Optional Parameters Transmitted (ADS-L)</dt>
    <dd>None. The Traffic and Status payloads carry no optional parameters, and no secure signature (E.4) is appended.</dd>
    <dt>Receive capabilities</dt>
    <dd>M-band, 868.2&nbsp;MHz from 450 to 820&nbsp;ms and 868.4&nbsp;MHz from 830 to 1200&nbsp;ms of every UTC second, 370&nbsp;ms on each channel. Over the direct slot, 450 to 1000&nbsp;ms, the average dwell is 49&nbsp;% across the two channels, declared as Partial (G.2.2). O-band HDR, 869.525&nbsp;MHz, from 210 to 440&nbsp;ms of every second, 230&nbsp;ms in the uplink slot, for the Traffic Uplink. O-band LDR is not received.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p>The manufacturer additionally declares that:</p>
  <ul class="declaration-statements">
    <li>Robust design processes and production controls are in place during manufacturing to ensure consistent quality and compliance with the applicable standard,</li>
    <li>The product&rsquo;s hardware, the LilyGO T-Echo, has passed CE testing for radio, EMC, safety and health under the Radio Equipment Directive 2014/53/EU (attestation of conformity SZ1220803-35313E-RF, BACL Shenzhen, 18 November 2022),</li>
    <li>The product uses an approved address range (Section ADS-L.4.SRD860.F.2.2)</li>
    <li>The product nominally transmits at least the &ldquo;Traffic&rdquo; and &ldquo;Status&rdquo; payloads (Subpart G)</li>
  </ul>

